===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|acre}}, {{m|enm|aker}}, from {{inh|en|ang|æcer||field where crops are grown}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*akr}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*akraz||field}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*h₂éǵros||field}}.

Cognate with {{cog|sco|acre}}, {{m|sco|aker}}, {{m|sco|acker||acre, field, arable land}}, {{cog|frr|ecir||field, a measure of land}}, {{cog|fy|eker||field}}, {{cog|nl|akker||field}}, {{cog|de|Acker||field, acre}}, {{cog|no|åker||field}} and {{cog|sv|åker||field}}, {{cog|is|akur||field}}, {{cog|la|ager||land, field, acre, countryside}}, {{cog|grc|ἀγρός||field}}, {{cog|sa|अज्र|tr=ájra||field, plain}}.

